 This method raises a ``sqlite_utils.db.TransformError`` exception if the table cannot be transformed, usually because there are existing constraints or indexes that are incompatible with modifications to the columns.
 
+When foreign keys are enabled, transforming a table inside an existing transaction raises ``sqlite_utils.db.TransactionError`` if that table is referenced by an ``ON DELETE CASCADE``, ``ON DELETE SET NULL`` or ``ON DELETE SET DEFAULT`` foreign key. This prevents the temporary ``DROP TABLE`` from applying those actions to referencing rows. Self-referential foreign keys are included. Transform the table outside the existing transaction, or disable foreign key enforcement before starting the transaction. Non-destructive inbound foreign keys and foreign keys from the transformed table to another table are unaffected.
+
 .. note::
     In the CLI: :ref:`sqlite-utils transform <cli_transform_table>`
 
